  "response": "**Calculation:**\n\n- Prevalence: P(D) = 1/500 = 0.002, P(¬D) = 0.998\n- Sensitivity: P(+|D) = 0.98\n- Specificity: P(−|¬D) = 0.95 → P(+|¬D) = 0.05\n\nUsing Bayes' theorem:\n\nP(+) = P(+|D)·P(D) + P(+|¬D)·P(¬D)\nP(+) = (0.98 × 0.002) + (0.05 × 0.998)\nP(+) = 0.00196 + 0.0499\nP(+) = 0.05186\n\nP(D|+) = P(+|D)·P(D) / P(+) = 0.00196 / 0.05186 ≈ 0.037794\n\nSo the probability that the person actually has the condition, given a positive test, is about **3.78%** — even with a fairly accurate test, most positives are false positives because the condition is rare.\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 3.78",
